        <mxCell id="gaps_hdr" value="GAPS & EXPLANATIONS — PARTIAL / NOT FOUND / CONCEPT ITEMS" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#723377;strokeColor=#723377;fontColor=#FFFFFF;fontStyle=1;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="950" width="1290" height="25" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="gap1" value="[1] Conditional Access for Agents — Entra (PARTIAL): GA for delegated-access agents (acting on behalf of user). Public preview for own-access agents (operating with own identity, not tied to user session). Requires Microsoft Agent 365 license ($15/user/month) + Entra P1 or M365 E3." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=8;fontColor=#555555;fillColor=#FBFBF9;strokeColor=#E5E5E5;spacingLeft=4;spacingRight=4;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="985" width="630" height="60" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="gap2" value="[2] Policy-as-Code — OPA/OpenFGA (NOT STARTED): NHIDecision.pdf confirms direction identified (OPA / OpenFGA / SpiceDB) but nothing built. GitOps policy changes, CI/CD-driven entitlement management, and automated onboarding (Entra, CEL expressions, gateway config) are patterns identified — automation not built. T-shirt size: S." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=8;fontColor=#555555;fillColor=#FBFBF9;strokeColor=#E5E5E5;spacingLeft=4;spacingRight=4;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="670" y="985" width="650" height="60" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="gap3" value="[3] AI Gateway Governance — Foundry (PREVIEW): Routes MCP traffic through Azure API Management for auth, rate limits, IP restrictions, audit logging. Only new MCP tools created in Foundry portal are routed. Tools using Managed OAuth are excluded. Existing tools not automatically mediated. Requires API Management instance connected to Foundry resource." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=8;fontColor=#555555;fillColor=#FBFBF9;strokeColor=#E5E5E5;spacingLeft=4;spacingRight=4;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1055" width="630" height="65" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="gap4" value="[4] Guardrails — Foundry (PARTIAL): Content safety controls are GA — screens prompts/responses for harmful content, prompt injection, hate/violence/self-harm. Network egress controls are PREVIEW — allow/deny/transform/rewrite actions, FQDN matching, header manipulation, audit mode, enforce mode, fail-closed evaluation." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=8;fontColor=#555555;fillColor=#FBFBF9;strokeColor=#E5E5E5;spacingLeft=4;spacingRight=4;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="670" y="1055" width="650" height="65" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="gap5" value="[5] Token Broker — CONCEPT ONLY: NHIDecision.pdf page 3 confirms: delegated OAuth, per-user token brokerage, downstream credential exchange. Required under either option (with or without Oasis). Oasis may assist with access governance but Pantheon still needs to broker downstream access. T-shirt size: S. No platform provides this out of box." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=8;fontColor=#555555;fillColor=#FBFBF9;strokeColor=#E5E5E5;spacingLeft=4;spacingRight=4;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1130" width="630" height="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="gap6" value="[6] Telemetry Pipeline — Dynatrace + Splunk (PARTIAL): NHIDecision.pdf page 4 confirms Dynatrace and Splunk integrations are in discovery stage — required under either option. Already logging inside Platform. PostgreSQL audit store exists. Prompt-to-action traceability and compliance reporting not yet built. T-shirt size: XS." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=8;fontColor=#555555;fillColor=#FBFBF9;strokeColor=#E5E5E5;spacingLeft=4;spacingRight=4;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="670" y="1130" width="650" height="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="gap7" value="[7] OBO / Delegated OAuth — Oasis (NOT FOUND): Oasis AAM product pages do not mention OBO flow, delegated OAuth, or user-delegated token exchange. Foundry provides OAuth Identity Passthrough (GA) — user authorizes once, Foundry stores/refreshes credentials, each downstream call runs as the user. Entra provides native OAuth 2.0 OBO." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=8;fontColor=#555555;fillColor=#FBFBF9;strokeColor=#E5E5E5;spacingLeft=4;spacingRight=4;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1210" width="630" height="65" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="gap8" value="[8] MCP Authentication — Oasis (NOT FOUND): Oasis AAM pages do not mention MCP authentication, MCP server connections, or MCP-specific auth. Foundry supports 7 auth types (GA): key-based, Entra Agent Identity, Project Managed Identity, OAuth Identity Passthrough, Managed OAuth, Custom OAuth, Unauthenticated." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=8;fontColor=#555555;fillColor=#FBFBF9;strokeColor=#E5E5E5;spacingLeft=4;spacingRight=4;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="670" y="1210" width="650" height="65" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="gap9" value="[9] A2A AuthZ — Oasis (NOT FOUND), Foundry (PARTIAL): Foundry supports A2A protocol v1.0 (GA) and v0.3 (preview) for agent-to-agent connectivity. But this is protocol-level, not authorization-level. A2A authorization (agent + user permission intersection, least-privilege decisions) requires custom work per NHIDecision.pdf. Agent Gateway extension — required under either option." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=8;fontColor=#555555;fillColor=#FBFBF9;strokeColor=#E5E5E5;spacingLeft=4;spacingRight=4;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1285" width="630" height="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="gap10" value="[10] Prompt-to-Action Audit Trail — Entra (PARTIAL): Entra provides sign-in logs and audit logs attributing actions to the agent identity (Agent ID). But Entra does not capture the prompt that triggered the action, the intent derived, or the policy decision made. Oasis provides full chain: Human to Agent to Prompt to Intent to Policy to Identity to Actions to Results." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=8;fontColor=#555555;fillColor=#FBFBF9;strokeColor=#E5E5E5;spacingLeft=4;spacingRight=4;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="670" y="1285" width="650" height="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="gap11" value="[11] PAM Escalation — Entra (PARTIAL), Foundry (NO): Entra access packages can have expiry dates and require sponsor approval for extension — time-bound access. But this is entitlement management, not context-aware PAM escalation triggered by business context and risk level at runtime. Oasis provides time-bound, policy-driven elevation triggered only when context and risk require it. Foundry has no PAM capability." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=8;fontColor=#555555;fillColor=#FBFBF9;strokeColor=#E5E5E5;spacingLeft=4;spacingRight=4;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1365" width="630" height="75" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="gap12" value="[12] ITDR / Anomaly Detection — Entra (PARTIAL): Entra ID Protection for agents detects risky identity behavior (accessing unfamiliar resources, high sign-in attempts). But this is identity-level risk scoring, not full ITDR. Oasis Scout uses AuthPrint to match anomalies against known threat actor fingerprints, detect compromised tokens across public/private channels, and trigger automated revocation." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=8;fontColor=#555555;fillColor=#FBFBF9;strokeColor=#E5E5E5;spacingLeft=4;spacingRight=4;spacingTop=2;spacingBottom=2;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="670" y="1365" width="650" height="75" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
